          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Henry Ford</strong><br>\nHenry Ford was born on July 30, 1863, on a farm in Greenfield Township, Michigan. His childhood years were spent attending a one-room school and doing farm work. From an early age, Ford showed an interest in mechanics by dismantling and reassembling timepieces. His natural curiosity led him to Detroit at the age of 16, where he worked as an apprentice machinist.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ford's Early Career</strong><br>\nBefore founding Ford Motor Company, Henry Ford was an engineer with the Edison Illuminating Company in Detroit. This job gave him enough time and money to experiment with gasoline engines in his free time. His work led to the creation of the Detroit Automobile Company in 1899, which was short-lived but crucial in his journey towards automotive innovation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Ford Motor Company</strong><br>\nIn 1903, with the help of investors, Henry Ford founded the Ford Motor Company. The company's first car, the Model A, was a success, selling over 1,700 units. Ford focused on making cars affordable and efficient, believing they should be accessible to the general public, not just the wealthy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
