            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Model T Revolution</strong><br>\nThe introduction of the Model T in 1908 changed the automotive industry forever. It was simple, sturdy, and versatile, appealing to the masses. Priced at $825, it was affordable for many Americans, and its popularity led to mass production, which further decreased the cost over time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Assembly Line Innovation</strong><br>\nHenry Ford pioneered the moving assembly line in 1913, revolutionizing manufacturing. This method cut the production time of a car from more than 12 hours to about two and a half hours. The innovation significantly dropped costs, making the Model T even more affordable and increasing its dominance in the market.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ford's $5 Workday</strong><br>\nIn 1914, Ford made another bold move by doubling his workers' pay to $5 a day. This increased productivity and reduced turnover rates. It also helped create a middle class with purchasing power to buy the products they made, a concept that was revolutionary at the time.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
